menu "Input device board resources"

    config APP_LOCAL_SPEAKER_TEST
        bool "One bounded local speaker tone before media startup"
        default n
        help
            Diagnostic image only: boot once plays three seconds of local
            1 kHz mono PCM through the actual board codec, without USB audio
            input or microphone capture. A physical button/lock skips or
            cancels the tone. The normal media owner starts only after the
            test confirms codec shutdown. No settings are persisted and no
            public remote audio-test API is enabled by this option.

    config APP_IMU_CAPTURE
        bool "Bounded raw IMU diagnostic capture"
        default n
        help
            Observe accepted ordered board samples in a fixed PSRAM buffer.
            A Mouse Motion rising edge begins a capture; disabling Motion or
            filling 6000 records ends it. Records are formatted and dumped
            later through the existing diagnostic console, at most one per
            coordinator loop. The observer never changes motion policy or
            reads the sensor. Full storage stops capture, not mouse input.
            This is a diagnostic build option, not a new motion estimator.

    config APP_DISPLAY_SPI_QUEUE_DEPTH
        int "Mosaico display SPI transaction queue ceiling"
        range 1 2
        default 1
        help
            Limit queued transactions for the Mosaico CO5300 panel only.
            The pinned BSP uses PSRAM draw buffers with internal DMA bounce
            buffers. The bus request remains capped at 4092 bytes, while the
            max-length query consumed by the LCD driver is capped at 2048 bytes
            after descriptor rounding. A ceiling of one retains at most 2048
            payload bytes; two permits 4096, plus allocator metadata. Smaller
            hardware limits still apply. The SDK recycles chunks while sending
            the entire viewport and preserves TE and final completion semantics.
            Increasing this ceiling requires a complete internal/DMA memory
            budget and device throughput qualification.

endmenu
